re_margins":66.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.004369051343079579,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":6.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.06630144695603679,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.35212403231501344,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0070200004,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a commercial-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the rare neuroendocrine diseases in the United States and internationally. The company's lead product candidate is IMCIVREE (setmelanotide), a rare melanocortin-4 receptor for the treatment of pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC), proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 1, leptin receptor (LEPR) deficiency obesity, Bardet-Biedl and Alstr\u00f6m syndrome, Prader-Willi syndrome, and hypothalamic obesity. It is in Phase 3 clinical trials for treating acquired hypothalamic obesity, congenital hypothalamic obesity, pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC) and LEPR insufficiency obesities, SRC1 deficiency obesity, and SH2B1 deficiency obesity; and in phase 2 clinical trails for the treatment of Prader-Willi syndrome and MC4R deficiency. The company is also developing bivamelagon, an investigational oral small molecule MC4R agonist that is in phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of MC4R pathway diseases; and RM-718, a next generation MC4R peptide agonist that is in phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of hypothalamic obesity. The company was formerly known as Rhythm Metabolic, Inc. and changed its name to Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. in October 2015. Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. David P. Meeker M.D. | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 414 people. Revenue per employee of $458K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $161K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Rhythm Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.8B market cap on $190M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +100% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $117M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 35% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 101% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $39.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 382% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (20.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:RYTM) Stock: Insider Christophe Jean Sells 10,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/rhythm-pharmaceuticals-nasdaqrytm-stock-insider-christophe-jean-sells-10000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795167526.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Rhythm Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:RYTM) vs. Senti Biosciences (NASDAQ:SNTI) Head to Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/rhythm-pharmaceuticals-nasdaqrytm-vs-senti-biosciences-nasdaqsnti-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794792530.0,"origin":"